<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="ZEC" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">Zechariah</para>
  <para style="mt">Zechariah</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the eighth month, in the second year of Daryavesh <char style="pn">(Darius)</char> <char style="add">[lord]</char>, came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, the son of Berekhyah <char style="add">[Yehovah blesses]</char>, the son of ‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness]</char> the prophet, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has been sore displeased with your fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Therefore say you<char style="ord">i</char> unto them, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Turn you<char style="ord">2f</char> unto me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and I will turn unto you, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Be you<char style="ord">2f</char> not as your fathers, unto whom the former prophets have cried, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Turn you<char style="ord">2f</char> now from your evil ways, and <char style="add">[from]</char> your evil doings: but they did not hear, nor hearken unto me, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Your fathers, where <char style="add">[are]</char> they? and the prophets, do they live forever?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But my words and my statutes, which I commanded my servants the prophets, did they not take hold of your fathers? and they returned and said, Like as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> thought to do unto us, according to our ways, and according to our doings, so has he dealt with us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Upon the four and twentieth day of the eleventh month, which <char style="add">[is]</char> the month Sh’vat <char style="add">[a rod]</char>, in the second year of Daryavesh <char style="pn">(Darius)</char> <char style="add">[lord]</char>, came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, the son of Berekhyah <char style="add">[Yehovah blesses]</char>, the son of ‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness]</char> the prophet, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />I saw by night, and behold a man riding upon a red horse, and he stood among the myrtle trees that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the bottom; and behind him <char style="add">[were there]</char> red horses, speckled, and white.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then said I, O my lord, what <char style="add">[are]</char> these? And the angel that talked with me said unto me, I will show you<char style="ord">i</char> what these <char style="add">[be]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the man that stood among the myrtle trees answered and said, These <char style="add">[are they]</char> whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has sent to walk to and fro through the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they answered the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that stood among the myrtle trees, and said, We have walked to and fro through the earth, and, behold, all the earth sits still, and is at rest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> answered and said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, how long will you<char style="ord">i</char> not have mercy on Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and on the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, against which you<char style="ord">i</char> have had indignation these threescore and ten years?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> answered the angel that talked with me <char style="add">[with]</char> good words <char style="add">[and]</char> comfortable words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So the angel that communed with me said unto me, Cry you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; I am jealous for Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and for Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char> with a great jealousy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And I am very sore displeased with the heathen <char style="add">[that are]</char> at ease: for I was but a little displeased, and they helped forward the affliction.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Therefore thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; I am returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> with mercies: my house shall be built in it, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and a line shall be stretched forth upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Cry yet, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; My cities through prosperity shall yet be spread abroad; and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall yet comfort Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>, and shall yet choose Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then lifted I up my eyes, and saw, and behold four horns.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And I said unto the angel that talked with me, What <char style="add">[be]</char> these? And he answered me, These <char style="add">[are]</char> the horns which have scattered Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> showed me four carpenters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then said I, What come these to do? And he spoke, saying, These <char style="add">[are]</char> the horns which have scattered Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, so that no man did lift up his head: but these are come to frighten <char style="pn">(make afriad)</char> them, to cast out the horns of the Gentiles, which lifted up <char style="add">[their]</char> horn over the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to scatter it.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />I lifted up my eyes again, and looked, and behold a man with a measuring line in his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then said I, Where go you<char style="ord">i</char>? And he said unto me, To measure Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to see what <char style="add">[is]</char> the breadth thereof, and what <char style="add">[is]</char> the length thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And, behold, the angel that talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And said unto him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall be inhabited <char style="add">[as]</char> towns without walls for the multitude of men and cattle in it:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For I, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, will be unto her a wall of fire round about, and will be the glory in the midst of her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Ho, ho, <char style="add">[come forth]</char>, and flee from the land of the north, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the heaven, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Deliver yourself, O Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>, that dwell <char style="add">[with]</char> the daughter of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; After the glory has he sent me unto the nations which spoiled you: for he that touches you touches the apple of his eye.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For, behold, I will shake my hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> to their servants: and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> has sent me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And many nations shall be joined to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in that day, and shall be my people: and I will dwell in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> has sent me unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall inherit Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> his portion in the holy land, and shall choose Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Be silent, O all flesh, before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for he is raised up out of his holy habitation.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And he showed me Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the High Priest standing before the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and Satan <char style="pn">(the adversary)</char> standing at his right hand to accuse him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Satan, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> rebuke <char style="pn">(reprimand; strongly warn; restrain)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, O Satan; even the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that has chosen Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> rebuke <char style="pn">(reprimand; strongly warn; restrain)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>: <char style="add">[is]</char> not this a brand plucked out of the fire?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> was clothed with filthy garments, and stood before the angel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he answered and spoke unto those that stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy garments from him. And unto him he said, Behold, I have caused your<char style="ord">i</char> iniquity to pass from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and I will clothe you<char style="ord">i</char> with change fine clothes</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And I said, Let them set a fair mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char> upon his head. So they set a fair mitre <char style="pn">(turban; ceremonial headdress)</char> upon his head, and clothed him with garments. And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> stood by.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> protested unto Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; If you<char style="ord">i</char> will walk in my ways, and if you<char style="ord">i</char> will keep my charge, then you<char style="ord">i</char> shall also judge my house, and shall also keep my courts, and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> free access to walk among these that stand by.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Hear now, O Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the High Priest, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and your<char style="ord">i</char> fellows that sit before you<char style="ord">i</char>: for they <char style="add">[are]</char> men wondered at: for, behold, I will bring forth My servant the BRANCH.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For behold the stone that I have laid before Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char>; upon one stone <char style="add">[shall be]</char> seven eyes: behold, I will engrave the graving thereof, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />In that day, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> call every man his neighbour under the vine and under the fig tree.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the angel that talked with me came again, and waked me, as a man that is wakened out of his sleep,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And said unto me, What see you<char style="ord">i</char>? And I said, I have looked, and behold a candlestick all <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, with a bowl upon the top of it, and his seven lamps thereon, and seven pipes to the seven lamps, which <char style="add">[are]</char> upon the top thereof:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And two olive trees by it, one upon the right <char style="add">[side]</char> of the bowl, and the other upon the left <char style="add">[side]</char> thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />So I answered and spoke to the angel that talked with me, saying, What <char style="add">[are]</char> these, my lord?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then the angel that talked with me answered and said unto me, Know you<char style="ord">i</char> not what these be? And I said, No, my lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then he answered and spoke unto me, saying, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char>, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Who <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, O great mountain? before Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char> [you<char style="ord">i</char> shall become] a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone <char style="add">[thereof with]</char> shoutings, <char style="add">[crying]</char>, Grace, grace unto it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Moreover the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The hands of Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon]</char> have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> has sent me unto you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />For who has despised the day of small things? for they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Z’rubavel <char style="add">[sown in Babylon] [with]</char> those seven; they <char style="add">[are]</char> the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which run to and fro through the whole earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then answered I, and said unto him, What <char style="add">[are]</char> these two olive trees upon the right <char style="add">[side]</char> of the candlestick and upon the left <char style="add">[side]</char> thereof?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And I answered again, and said unto him, What <char style="add">[be these]</char> two olive branches which through the two golden pipes empty the golden <char style="add">[oil]</char> out of themselves?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he answered me and said, Know you<char style="ord">i</char> not what these <char style="add">[be]</char>? And I said, No, my lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then said he, These <char style="add">[are]</char> the two anointed ones, that stand by the Lord-Adon of the whole earth.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then I turned, and lifted up my eyes, and looked, and behold a flying scroll.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he said unto me, What see you<char style="ord">i</char>? And I answered, I see a flying scroll; the length thereof <char style="add">[is]</char> 30 feet, and the breadth thereof fifteen feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then said he unto me, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the curse that goes forth over the face of the whole earth: for everyone that steals shall be cut off <char style="add">[as]</char> on this side according to it; and everyone that swears shall be cut off <char style="add">[as]</char> on that side according to it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />I will bring it forth, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and it shall enter into the house of the thief, and into the house of him that swears falsely by my name: and it shall remain in the midst of his house, and shall consume it with the timber thereof and the stones thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then the angel that talked with me went forth, and said unto me, Lift up now your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, and see what <char style="add">[is]</char> this that goes forth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I said, What <char style="add">[is]</char> it? And he said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> an eifah that goes forth. He said moreover, This <char style="add">[is]</char> their resemblance through all the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And, behold, there was lifted up a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> of lead: and this <char style="add">[is]</char> a woman that sits in the midst of the eifah.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he said, This <char style="add">[is]</char> wickedness. And he cast it into the midst of the eifah; and he cast the weight of lead upon the mouth thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then lifted I up my eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came out two women, and the wind <char style="add">[was]</char> in their wings; for they had wings like the wings of a stork: and they lifted up the eifah between the earth and the heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then said I to the angel that talked with me, Where do these bear the eifah?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he said unto me, To build it an house in the land of Shin’ar <char style="add">[country of two rivers]</char>: and it shall be established, and set there upon her own base.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And I turned, and lifted up my eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came four chariots out from between two mountains; and the mountains <char style="add">[were]</char> mountains of brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />In the first chariot <char style="add">[were]</char> red horses; and in the second chariot black horses;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And in the third chariot white horses; and in the fourth chariot grizzled and bay horses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then I answered and said unto the angel that talked with me, What <char style="add">[are]</char> these, my lord?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the angel answered and said unto me, These <char style="add">[are]</char> the four spirits of the heavens, which go forth from standing before the Lord-Adon of all the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />The black horses which <char style="add">[are]</char> in it go forth into the north country; and the white go forth after them; and the grizzled go forth toward the south country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the bay went forth, and sought to go that they might walk to and fro through the earth: and he said, Get you hence, walk to and fro through the earth. So they walked to and fro through the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Then cried he upon me, and spoke unto me, saying, Behold, these that go toward the north country have quieted my spirit in the north country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Take of <char style="add">[them of]</char> the captivity, <char style="add">[even]</char> of Heldai <char style="add">[worldly]</char>, of Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, and of Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char>, which are come from Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and come you<char style="ord">i</char> the same day, and go into the house of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> the son of Tzefan’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has treasured]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then take silver and gold, and make crowns, and set <char style="add">[them]</char> upon the head of Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the son of Y’hotzadak <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char>, the High Priest;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And speak unto him, saying, Thus speaks the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, saying, Behold the man whose name <char style="add">[is]</char> The BRANCH; and he shall grow up out of his place, and he shall build the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Even he shall build the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and he shall bear the glory, and shall sit and rule upon his throne; and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the crowns shall be to Helem <char style="add">[strength or dream]</char>, and to Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, and to Y’da’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah has known]</char>, and to Hen the son of Tzefan’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has treasured]</char>, for a memorial in the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they <char style="add">[that are]</char> far off shall come and build in the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> has sent me unto you. And <char style="add">[this]</char> shall come to pass, if you<char style="ord">2f</char> will diligently obey the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the fourth year of king Daryavesh <char style="pn">(Darius)</char> <char style="add">[lord]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char> in the fourth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the ninth month, <char style="add">[even]</char> in Kislev <char style="add">[his confidence]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />When they had sent unto the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Sar’etzer <char style="add">[prince of fire]</char> and Regem-Melekh <char style="add">[king’s heap]</char>, and their men, to pray before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> to speak unto the priests which <char style="add">[were]</char> in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and to the prophets, saying, Should I weep in the fifth month, separating myself, as I have done these so many years?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Speak unto all the people of the land, and to the priests, saying, When you<char style="ord">2f</char> fasted and mourned in the fifth and seventh <char style="add">[month]</char>, even those seventy years, did you<char style="ord">2f</char> at all fast unto me, <char style="add">[even]</char> to me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And when you<char style="ord">2f</char> did eat, and when you<char style="ord">2f</char> did drink, did not you<char style="ord">2f</char> eat <char style="add">[for yourselves]</char>, and drink <char style="add">[for yourselves]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Should you<char style="ord">2f</char>]</char> not <char style="add">[hear]</char> the words which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has cried by the former prophets, when Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> was inhabited and in prosperity, and the cities thereof round about her, when <char style="add">[men]</char> inhabited the south and the plain?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Thus speaks the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, saying, Execute true judgment, and show mercy and compassions every man to his brother:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And oppress not the widow, nor the fatherless, the stranger, nor the poor; and let none of you imagine evil against his brother in your heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But they refused to hearken, and pulled away the shoulder, and stopped their ears, that they should not hear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Yes, they made their hearts <char style="add">[as]</char> an adamant stone, lest they should hear the law, and the words which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> has sent in his spirit by the former prophets: therefore came a great wrath from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Therefore it is come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> as he cried, and they would not hear; so they cried, and I would not hear, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But I scattered them with a whirlwind among all the nations whom they knew not. Thus the land was desolate after them, that no man passed through nor returned: for they laid the pleasant land desolate.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Again the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> came <char style="add">[to me]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; I was jealous for Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char> with great jealousy, and I was jealous for her with great fury.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; I am returned unto Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>, and will dwell in the midst of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall be called a city of truth; and the mountain of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> the holy mountain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; There shall yet old men and old women dwell in the streets of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and every man with his staff in his hand for very age.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the streets of the city shall be full of boys and girls playing in the streets thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; If it be marvelous in the eyes of the remnant of this people in these days, should it also be marvelous in my eyes? says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Behold, I will save my people from the east country, and from the west country;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I will bring them, and they shall dwell in the midst of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, in tand in righteousness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; Let your hands be strong, you<char style="ord">2f</char> that hear in these days these words by the mouth of the prophets, which <char style="add">[were]</char> in the day <char style="add">[that]</char> the foundation of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> was laid, that the temple might be built.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />For before these days there was no hire for man, nor any hire for beast; neither <char style="add">[was there any]</char> peace to him that went out or came in because of the affliction: for I set all men everyone against his neighbour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But now I <char style="add">[will]</char> not <char style="add">[be]</char> unto the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of this people as in the former days, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />For the seed <char style="add">[shall be]</char> prosperous; the vine shall give her fruit, and the ground shall give her increase, and the heavens shall give their dew; and I will cause the remnant of this people to possess all these <char style="add">[things]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> as you<char style="ord">2f</char> were a curse among the heathen, O house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; so will I save you, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall be a blessing: fear not, <char style="add">[but]</char> let your hands be strong.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />For thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; As I thought to punish you, when your fathers provoked me to wrath, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and I repented not:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So again have I thought in these days to do well unto Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and to the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: fear you<char style="ord">2f</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />These <char style="add">[are]</char> the things that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall do; Speak you<char style="ord">2f</char> every man the tto his neighbour; execute the judgment of tand peace in your gates:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And let none of you imagine evil in your hearts against his neighbour; and love no false oath: for all these <char style="add">[are things]</char> that I hate, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> came unto me, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; The fast of the fourth <char style="add">[month]</char>, and the fast of the fifth, and the fast of the seventh, and the fast of the tenth, shall be to the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> joy and gladness, and cheerful feasts; therefore love the tand peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; <char style="add">[It shall]</char> yet <char style="add">[come to pass]</char>, that there shall come people, and the inhabitants of many cities:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the inhabitants of one <char style="add">[city]</char> shall go to another, saying, Let us go speedily to pray before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>: I will go also.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Yes, many people and strong nations shall come to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and to pray before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>; In those days <char style="add">[it shall come to pass]</char>, that ten men shall take hold out of all languages of the nations, even shall take hold of the skirt of him that is Jewish (Y’hudi), saying, We will go with you: for we have heard <char style="add">[that]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [is]</char> with you.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The burden of the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the land of Hadrakh <char style="add">[dwelling]</char>, and Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver] [shall be]</char> the rest thereof: when the eyes of man, as of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[shall be]</char> toward the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> also shall border thereby; Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, and Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, though it be very wise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyrus)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> did build herself a strong hold, and heaped up silver as the dust, and fine gold as the mire of the streets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Behold, the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All]</char> will cast her out, and he will strike her power in the sea; and she shall be devoured with fire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Ashkelon [The Fire of Infamy: I shall be Weighed] shall see <char style="add">[it]</char>, and fear; ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char> also <char style="add">[shall see it]</char>, and be very sorrowful, and ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char>; for her expectation shall be ashamed; and the king shall perish from ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, and Ashkelon <char style="add">[The Fire of Infamy: I shall be Weighed]</char> shall not be inhabited.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And a child of incest shall dwell in Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and I will cut off the pride of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I will take away his blood out of his mouth, and his abominations from between his teeth: but he that remains, even he, <char style="add">[shall be]</char> for our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and he shall be as a governor in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and ‘Ekron <char style="add">[Torn Up by the Roots]</char> as a Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And I will encamp about my house because of the army, because of him that passes by, and because of him that returns: and no oppressor shall pass through them any more: for now have I seen with my eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>; shout, O daughter of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: behold, your<char style="ord">i</char> King comes unto you<char style="ord">i</char>: he <char style="add">[is]</char> just, and having Salvation; lowly, and riding upon an ass, and upon a colt the foal of an ass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And I will cut off the chariot from Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and the horse from Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and the battle bow shall be cut off: and he shall speak peace unto the heathen: and his dominion <char style="add">[shall be]</char> from sea <char style="add">[even]</char> to sea, and from the river <char style="add">[even]</char> to the ends of the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />As for you<char style="ord">i</char> also, by the blood of your<char style="ord">i</char> covenant I have sent forth your<char style="ord">i</char> prisoners out of the pit wherein <char style="add">[is]</char> no water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Turn you to the strong hold, you<char style="ord">2f</char> prisoners of hope: even today do I declare <char style="add">[that]</char> I will render double unto you<char style="ord">i</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />When I have bent Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> for me, filled the bow with Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and raised up you<char style="ord">i</char> sons, O Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>, against you<char style="ord">i</char> sons, O Greece, and made you<char style="ord">i</char> as the sword of a mighty man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall be seen over them, and his arrow shall go forth as the lightning: and the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> shall blow the trumpet, and shall go with whirlwinds of the south.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> shall defend them; and they shall devour, and subdue with sling stones; and they shall drink, <char style="add">[and]</char> make a noise as through wine; and they shall be filled like bowls, <char style="add">[and]</char> as the corners of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shall save them in that day as the flock of his people: for they <char style="add">[shall be as]</char> the stones of a crown, lifted up as an flag <char style="pn">(or banner; as of an army)</char> upon his land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />For how great <char style="add">[is]</char> his goodness, and how great <char style="add">[is]</char> his beauty! corn shall make the young men cheerful, and New Wine the maids.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Ask you<char style="ord">2f</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> rain in the time of the latter rain; <char style="add">[so]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall make bright clouds, and give them showers of rain, to everyone grass in the field.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For the idols have spoken vanity, and the diviners have seen a lie, and have told false dreams; they comfort in vain: therefore they went their way as a flock, they were troubled, because <char style="add">[there was]</char> no shepherd.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Mine anger was kindled against the shepherds, and I punished the goats: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> has visited his flock the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and has made them as his goodly horse in the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Out of him came forth the corner, out of him the nail, out of him the battle bow, out of him every oppressor together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they shall be as mighty <char style="add">[men]</char>, which trample down <char style="add">[their enemies]</char> in the mire of the streets in the battle: and they shall fight, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> with them, and the riders on horses shall be confounded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And I will strengthen the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and I will save the house of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>, and I will bring them again to place them; for I have mercy upon them: and they shall be as though I had not cast them off: for I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and will hear them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And <char style="add">[they of]</char> Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> shall be like a mighty <char style="add">[man]</char>, and their heart shall rejoice as through wine: yes, their children shall see <char style="add">[it]</char>, and be glad; their heart shall rejoice in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />I will hiss for them, and gather them; for I have redeemed them: and they shall increase as they have increased.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And I will sow them among the people: and they shall remember me in far countries; and they shall live with their children, and turn again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />I will bring them again also out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and gather them out of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>; and I will bring them into the land of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char> and L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>; and <char style="add">[place]</char> shall not be found for them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he shall pass through the sea with affliction, and shall strike the waves in the sea, and all the deeps of the river shall dry up: and the pride of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> shall be brought down, and the scepter of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> shall depart away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And I will strengthen them in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and they shall walk up and down in his name, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Open your<char style="ord">i</char> doors, O L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, that the fire may devour your<char style="ord">i</char> cedars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Howl, fir tree; for the cedar is fallen; because the mighty are spoiled: howl, O you<char style="ord">2f</char> oaks of Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char>; for the forest of the vintage is come down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There is]</char> a voice of the howling of the shepherds; for their glory is spoiled: a voice of the roaring of young lions; for the pride of Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> is spoiled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; Feed the flock of the slaughter;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Whose possessors slay them, and hold themselves not guilty: and they that sell them say, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for I am rich: and their own shepherds pity them not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For I will no more pity the inhabitants of the land, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: but, lo, I will deliver the men everyone into his neighbour’s hand, and into the hand of his king: and they shall strike the land, and out of their hand I will not deliver <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And I will feed the flock of slaughter, <char style="add">[even]</char> you, O poor of the flock. And I took unto me two rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char>; the one I called [No’am] Beauty, and the other I called <char style="add">[Hovalim]</char> Bound Together; and I fed the flock.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Three shepherds also I cut off in one month; and my soul loathed them, and their soul also abhorred me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then said I, I will not feed you: that that dies, let it die; and that that is to be cut off, let it be cut off; and let the rest eat everyone the flesh of another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And I took my staff, <char style="add">[even]</char> Beauty, and cut it asunder, that I might break my covenant which I had made with all the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it was broken in that day: and so the poor of the flock that waited upon me knew that it <char style="add">[was]</char> the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And I said unto them, If you<char style="ord">2f</char> think good, give <char style="add">[me]</char> my price; and if not, refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>. So they weighed for my price thirty <char style="add">[pieces]</char> of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto me, Cast it unto the potter: a goodly price that I was prized at of them. And I took the thirty <char style="add">[pieces]</char> of silver, and cast them to the potter in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then I cut asunder my other staff, <char style="add">[even]</char> Bands, that I might break the brotherhood between Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto me, Take unto yourselfi yet the instruments of a foolish shepherd.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For, lo, I will raise up a shepherd in the land, <char style="add">[which]</char> shall not visit those that be cut off, neither shall seek the young one, nor heal that that is broken, nor feed that that stands still: but he shall eat the flesh of the fat, and tear their claws in pieces.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Woe to the idol shepherd that leaves the flock! the sword <char style="add">[shall be]</char> upon his arm, and upon his right eye: his arm shall be clean dried up, and his right eye shall be utterly darkened.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />The burden of the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which stretches forth the heavens, and lays the foundation of the earth, and forms the spirit of man within him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Behold, I will make Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> a cup of trembling unto all the people round about, when they shall be in the siege both against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [and]</char> against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And in that day will I make Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> a burdensome stone for all people: all that burden themselves with it shall be cut in pieces, though all the people of the earth be gathered together against it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />In that day, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, I will strike every horse with astonishment, and his rider with madness: and I will open my eyes upon the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and will strike every horse of the people with blindness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the governors of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> shall say in their heart, The inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace] [shall be]</char> my strength in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />In that day will I make the governors of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> like an hearth of fire among the wood, and like a torch of fire in a sheaf; and they shall devour all the people round about, on the right hand and on the left: and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall be inhabited again in her own place, <char style="add">[even]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> also shall save the tents of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> first, that the glory of the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and the glory of the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> do not magnify <char style="add">[themselves]</char> against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />In that day shall the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> defend the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; and he that is feeble among them at that day shall be as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; and the house of David <char style="add">[beloved] [shall be]</char> as God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, as the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And it shall come to pass in that day, <char style="add">[that]</char> I will seek to destroy all the nations that come against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And I will pour upon the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and upon the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, the spirit of grace and of supplications: and they shall look upon me whom they have pierced, and they shall mourn for him, as one mourns for <char style="add">[his]</char> only <char style="add">[son]</char>, and shall be in bitterness for him, as one that is in bitterness for <char style="add">[his]</char> firstborn.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />In that day shall there be a great mourning in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, as the mourning of Hadad-Rimmon <char style="add">[Hadad of the pomegranates]</char> in the valley of Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char> n.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the land shall mourn, every family apart; the family of the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> apart, and their wives apart; the family of the house of Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> apart, and their wives apart;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />The family of the house of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char> apart, and their wives apart; the family of Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> apart, and their wives apart;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />All the families that remain, every family apart, and their wives apart.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In that day there shall be a fountain opened to the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and to the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> for sin and for uncleanness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it shall come to pass in that day, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> I will cut off the names of the idols out of the land, and they shall no more be remembered: and also I will cause the prophets and the unclean spirit to pass out of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> when any shall yet prophesy, then his father and his mother that begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> him shall say unto him, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not live; for you<char style="ord">i</char> speak lies in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and his father and his mother that begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> him shall thrust him through when he prophesies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it shall come to pass in that day, <char style="add">[that]</char> the prophets shall be ashamed every one of his vision, when he has prophesied; neither shall they wear a rough garment to deceive:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But he shall say, I <char style="add">[am]</char> no prophet, I <char style="add">[am]</char> an farmer; for man taught me to keep cattle from my youth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And <char style="add">[one]</char> shall say unto him, What <char style="add">[are]</char> these wounds in your<char style="ord">i</char> hands? Then he shall answer, <char style="add">[Those]</char> with which I was wounded <char style="add">[in]</char> the house of my friends.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Awake, O sword, against my shepherd, and against the man <char style="add">[that is]</char> my fellow, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>: strike the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered: and I will turn my hand upon the little ones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> in all the land, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, two parts in it shall be cut off <char style="add">[and]</char> die; but the third shall be left in it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And I will bring the third part through the fire, and will refine them as silver is refined, and will try them as gold is tried: they shall call on My Name, and I will hear them: I will say, It <char style="add">[is]</char> my people: and they shall say, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Behold, the day of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> comes, and you<char style="ord">i</char> spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> shall be divided in the midst of you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For I will gather all nations against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to battle; and the city shall be taken, and the houses rifled, and the women ravished; and half of the city shall go forth into captivity, and the residue <char style="pn">(part that remains, the rest)</char> of the people shall not be cut off from the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Then shall the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> go forth, and fight against those nations, as when he fought in the day of battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And his feet shall stand in that day upon the mount of Olives, which <char style="add">[is]</char> before Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> on the east, and the mount of Olives shall cleave <char style="pn">(split open; cut open; divide)</char> in the midst thereof toward the east and toward the west, <char style="add">[and there shall be]</char> a very great valley; and half of the mountain shall remove toward the north, and half of it toward the south.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall flee <char style="add">[to]</char> the valley of the mountains; for the valley of the mountains shall reach unto Atzel [proximity: he has reserved]: yes, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall flee, like as you<char style="ord">2f</char> fled from before the earthquake in the days of ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shall come, <char style="add">[and]</char> all the saints with you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it shall come to pass in that day, <char style="add">[that]</char> the light shall not be clear, <char style="add">[nor]</char> dark:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But it shall be one day which shall be known to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, not day, nor night: but it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> at evening time it shall be light.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it shall be in that day, <char style="add">[that]</char> living waters shall go out from Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; half of them toward the former sea, and half of them toward the hinder sea: in summer and in winter shall it be.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and his name one.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />All the land shall be turned as a plain from Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char> to Rimmon <char style="add">[Pomegranate]</char> south of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and it shall be lifted up, and inhabited in her place, from Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>’s gate unto the place of the first gate, unto the corner gate, and <char style="add">[from]</char> the tower of Hanan’el <char style="add">[God is favoured]</char> unto the king’s winepresses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And <char style="add">[men]</char> shall dwell in it, and there shall be no more utter destruction; but Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall be safely inhabited.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And this shall be the plague which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will strike all the people that have fought against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; Their flesh shall consume away while they stand upon their feet, and their eyes shall consume away in their holes, and their tongue shall consume away in their mouth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And it shall come to pass in that day, <char style="add">[that]</char> a great tumult from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall be among them; and they shall lay hold everyone on the hand of his neighbour, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> also shall fight at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; and the wealth of all the heathen round about shall be gathered together, gold, and silver, and apparel, in great abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And so shall be the plague of the horse, of the mule, of the camel, and of the ass, and of all the beasts that shall be in these tents, as this plague.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> everyone that is left of all the nations which came against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall even go up from year to year to worship the King, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, and to keep the feast of tabernacles.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> whoso will not come up of <char style="add">[all]</char> the families of the earth unto Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to worship the King, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>, even upon them shall be no rain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And if the family of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> go not up, and come not, that <char style="add">[have]</char> no <char style="add">[rain]</char>; there shall be the plague, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> will strike the heathen that come not up to keep the feast of tabernacles.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />This shall be the punishment of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and the punishment of all nations that come not up to keep the feast of tabernacles.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />In that day shall there be upon the bells of the horses, HOLINESS UNTO THE LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and the pots in the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> house shall be like the bowls before the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Yes, every pot in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> shall be holiness unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>: and all they that sacrifice shall come and take of them, and seethe in it: and in that day there shall be no more the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchants]</char> in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>.</para>
</usx>